1
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:35,210
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds…)

2
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,340
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,350
(Also, children and animals were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,110
{\an8}(Episode 14)

5
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:51,960
{\an8}It was a woman? Are you sure?

6
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,560
{\an8}You think I can't tell the difference
between a man and a woman?

7
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,130
{\an8}The man I saw before.

8
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,500
{\an8}He's Kingfisher.

9
00:00:57,670 --> 00:00:59,430
{\an8}I saw Kingfisher sniping,
and I was spotted.

10
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,240
{\an8}It's extremely rare
for a serial killer like Kingfisher...

11
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,310
{\an8}to suddenly abandon their principles.

12
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:06,340
{\an8}The suspect is believed
to be a woman in her 30s?

13
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:08,110
{\an8}What is this?

14
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,080
{\an8}What is it?

15
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:12,910
{\an8}I'm a little busy right now.

16
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:32,470
{\an8}(Blocked Number)

17
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:33,970
You're being dispatched? At this hour?

18
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,700
Where are you headed?

19
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,610
Seonyudo Island? With the SWAT team?
Wow, what a huge operation.

20
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,410
Be careful and don't get hurt.

21
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:48,220
Hey, when are you going to meet with me?
You said you'd be my sparring partner.

22
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,580
Well...

23
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,320
Where are you going?

24
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,320
Hey.

25
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:02,400
(My Big Treasure)

26
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,990
It's not fair. For the two of us.

27
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:35,300
We basically do the same job.

28
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,500
Listen, I'm warning you.

29
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:40,300
My husband, my child...

30
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:44,000
If you lay a single finger on them,

31
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,710
you'll find out
what a living hell feels like.

32
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:51,350
Oh, really?
Then you can go through a living hell too.

33
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:54,150
You can be completely destroyed too.

34
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,820
After losing everything you hold dear.

35
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,900
I wonder if you'll still be able
to act so high and mighty then.

36
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:41,260
I'm a step too late again.

37
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:04,750
(Police)

38
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,320
(Police)

39
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,260
(Police)

40
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:12,960
Let me repeat myself.

41
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,730
Capturing them alive is the priority.

42
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:16,800
Yes, sir. Attention, all personnel.

43
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,970
We must capture the suspect alive.
Understood?

44
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,300
Teams 1 and 2, this way. Team 3, that way.

45
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,510
Move in.

46
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:42,190
Why did you stop?

47
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:43,590
Go on.

48
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:46,830
Kill me.

49
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,860
In front of your husband.

50
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:51,200
Do what you're good at.

51
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,970
Suspected on the rooftop
of the building at 11 o'clock.

52
00:05:35,010 --> 00:05:37,410
This way. Team 1, with me.
Team 2, provide cover.

53
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,780
Move.

54
00:05:46,290 --> 00:05:47,290
Yu Bo Na.

55
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,060
Rot in prison for the rest of your life.

56
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:40,440
Dong Jin is here. We have to go.

57
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,550
We have to go. Quickly.

58
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,580
Hurry.

59
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:01,830
What is this? Did he know everything?

60
00:07:03,730 --> 00:07:06,270
If it's an unstoppable blade,
I hope it comes for me.

61
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:10,400
That the barrel of the gun
is aimed only at me.

62
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:21,180
Please secure the perimeter as well.

63
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,070
Honey.

64
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:43,070
Honey.

65
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,980
Honey, how...

66
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,920
- No. Honey.
- Ma'am.

67
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:09,460
So it was you, Leila.

68
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:12,900
Let's catch that woman.

69
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:25,710
She's not in the building.

70
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:27,350
She's not here either.

71
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,660
North side of the park.

72
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:38,390
Suspect spotted in the area
near the Han River.

73
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:40,090
She's heading toward Seonyu Bridge.

74
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,860
All units, move to that location.

75
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:43,500
Darn it.

76
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:13,460
First, let's get out of here.

77
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:42,890
Suspect spotted. She's carrying
what appears to be a firearm.

78
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:44,390
Secure her before she exits the park.

79
00:09:58,670 --> 00:09:59,670
Darn it.

80
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,720
(No Entry)

81
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:21,160
The pleasure is all ours.
We appreciate the personal invitation.

82
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,370
So we meet like this.

83
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,800
Follow me.

84
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:32,870
This way.

85
00:10:34,570 --> 00:10:35,710
Be careful, it's slippery.

86
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,600
It looks like
Kwon Tae Sung made his choice.

87
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,170
Now it's Yu Bo Na's turn.

88
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,180
Freeze.

89
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,720
Police. Don't move.

90
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:29,030
Drop the gun and put your hands up.

91
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:31,030
Now.

92
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,130
It's over, Kingfisher.

93
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,840
Drop the gun.

94
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:40,270
Kingfisher?

95
00:11:42,710 --> 00:11:43,710
Yu Bo Na.

96
00:11:46,210 --> 00:11:48,020
You're so lucky.

97
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,550
Unbelievable.

98
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:08,270
Cease fire.

99
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:11,270
Cease fire.

100
00:12:40,830 --> 00:12:42,340
(Children Protection Zone)

101
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:46,670
As you know,

102
00:12:47,210 --> 00:12:48,780
we can't go to a regular hospital.

103
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:52,180
I know.

104
00:13:04,890 --> 00:13:06,730
(Bomyeong Clinic)

105
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:16,970
Get her inside, quickly.

106
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:22,180
Get everything ready. Now.

107
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:26,750
She'll be all right.

108
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:29,880
(Operating Room)

109
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:31,420
(No Entry)

110
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:34,250
Tae Sung.

111
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:38,960
There are people who help her out
when needed.

112
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,090
She's going to be okay.

113
00:13:42,830 --> 00:13:43,830
Okay.

114
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,340
(Operating Room)

115
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:06,820
(Operating Room)

116
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:27,170
Sit down.

117
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:51,030
Luckily, it only damaged muscle tissue
and missed her vitals.

118
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:54,900
She'll be fine with a little rest.

119
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:57,940
Thank you.

120
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:09,120
Sir.

121
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:13,290
The National Forensic Service
is on standby.

122
00:15:13,890 --> 00:15:15,190
Since this is such a major case,

123
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,760
the director himself
is performing the autopsy.

124
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:19,660
Looks like we'll be pulling an all-nighter
for the autopsy.

125
00:15:19,730 --> 00:15:21,560
Anything unusual happened
while you were on watch?

126
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,330
Any suspicious activity.

127
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,200
No, not really.

128
00:15:25,470 --> 00:15:26,670
Is something bothering you?

129
00:15:29,270 --> 00:15:30,270
I don't know.

130
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:33,870
I don't know if I missed something
or if I'm still missing something.

131
00:15:42,950 --> 00:15:44,080
Why did you do it?

132
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,460
Honey, why did you step in for me?

133
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:58,200
If something happens to you,
how am I supposed to live?

134
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:04,940
Without you, how... How can I go on?

135
00:16:43,110 --> 00:16:44,610
(Director Na Guk Jin)

136
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:47,410
(Director Na Guk Jin)

137
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:53,150
(New Message From Director Na Guk Jin)

138
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:57,720
Hey, Kwon Tae Sung.
Why aren't you answering my calls?

139
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,130
Don't tell me you're still sleeping.

140
00:16:59,330 --> 00:17:01,530
Kingfisher was shot and killed
by the police last night.

141
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,100
Hey, you need to get over there now.
The Forensic Service or Police Agency.

142
00:17:05,370 --> 00:17:08,700
Last night, the serial shooter
known as Kingfisher was killed.

143
00:17:09,970 --> 00:17:12,010
Rot in prison for the rest of your life.

144
00:17:17,110 --> 00:17:20,210
According to reports,
Kingfisher was in Seoul last night...

145
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,220
and was killed on site
following a police chase.

146
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,950
Kingfisher's identity,
which had been shrouded...

147
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,190
in mystery for the past 15 years,

148
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:28,320
was unexpectedly revealed
to be a woman in her 30s,

149
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,060
leaving the public in a state
of shock and confusion.

150
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:33,590
From the National Forensic Service?
Has Kingfisher's identity been confirmed?

151
00:17:33,730 --> 00:17:35,630
Who is it?
Please release the name and face.

152
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:37,200
Why was the suspect killed
and not captured alive?

153
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:40,030
Are you sure the woman in her 30s
who died at the scene is Kingfisher?

154
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:50,380
- Good work.
- You all worked hard.

155
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,150
Be careful lifting it.

156
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,150
(Special Investigation Team 2)

157
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:57,980
Good work.

158
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:00,690
But what do you mean
her identity can't be confirmed?

159
00:18:00,850 --> 00:18:04,220
Her fingerprints and DNA information
don't show up in the national database.

160
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:06,530
We also checked
with the immigration office,

161
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:09,460
but there are no
matching foreigner fingerprints.

162
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:11,500
So what,
she entered the country illegally?

163
00:18:12,330 --> 00:18:16,240
Well, for now, we've requested
an identity check through Interpol.

164
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:20,210
My goodness, nothing ever goes smoothly.

165
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:22,340
Still, it's a relief that we caught her.

166
00:18:23,910 --> 00:18:25,750
You did well. You also did well.

167
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:29,780
(Commissioner Shin Min Seok)

168
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,920
Everyone's going crazy.

169
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,020
Yes, Commissioner.

170
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,320
Honey.

171
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:07,250
Are you okay?

172
00:19:08,050 --> 00:19:09,060
Are you really okay?

173
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,490
You did well. You went through so much.

174
00:19:11,890 --> 00:19:14,090
Where are you hurting?
Are you uncomfortable anywhere?

175
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:16,060
Should I go get a doctor?

176
00:19:20,530 --> 00:19:21,840
Honey, if you get up...

177
00:19:28,110 --> 00:19:29,840
Can you get the Team Leader for me?

178
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:34,510
Okay.

179
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:42,920
Is Manager Yu all right? She's awake?

180
00:19:43,890 --> 00:19:44,890
Yes.

181
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,030
Bo Na is asking for the Team Leader.

182
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:01,470
(Hospital Room)

183
00:20:04,810 --> 00:20:07,950
Se Ah, I don't think
I can come home tonight.

184
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:10,720
Okay, then I'll have her sleep
at our place tonight.

185
00:20:11,050 --> 00:20:12,050
Okay, thank you.

186
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:21,560
(Hospital Room)

187
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:26,070
Honey, what are you doing?

188
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,700
Why? Are you trying to go somewhere?

189
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,870
You already knew, didn't you?

190
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,110
It was from that day.

191
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,980
The day Yul went to the emergency room.

192
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,380
You kept avoiding my gaze.

193
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:46,020
The day you looked at me
like I was a stranger.

194
00:20:53,030 --> 00:20:54,930
That's why you came home late for a while,

195
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,760
and you couldn't eat or sleep well.

196
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:01,800
- Honey, I...
- You must have had a really hard time.

197
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:03,340
Honey, just listen to me for a second.

198
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,600
You were angry too, weren't you?

199
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:08,440
At your wife who deceived you
for so long, right?

200
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,610
You must have been so confused...

201
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:14,810
and felt hopeless.

202
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:20,120
You're right.

203
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,220
I was angry,

204
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:27,630
and I was confused and felt hopeless.

205
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:32,830
Honestly, your secret was so heavy
that I was scared, but...

206
00:21:33,970 --> 00:21:35,970
I've come to only one conclusion.
To protect you.

207
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:40,440
To protect you and to protect our family.

208
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,180
Honey, let's just go back
to how we were, okay?

209
00:21:45,750 --> 00:21:46,810
We can laugh again...

210
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:51,320
You know, we can act
like nothing ever happened.

211
00:21:55,250 --> 00:21:56,690
Like nothing ever happened?

212
00:22:05,970 --> 00:22:07,300
I don't think I can do that.

213
00:22:12,810 --> 00:22:14,170
Every time you look at me,

214
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:16,310
you'll be reminded of
what kind of person I am.

215
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:18,710
I'll feel like a stranger to you,

216
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:20,310
and you'll be confused and tormented.

217
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,390
You'll be anxious every moment,
wondering...

218
00:22:26,390 --> 00:22:28,250
when something like this
will happen again.

219
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:29,890
No, that's not true at all.

220
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,560
I'll become your hell.

221
00:22:32,630 --> 00:22:35,600
No, honey. No, honey. Please, no.

222
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:45,770
I can't go back to the way I was.

223
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:51,210
You still don't really know me.

224
00:23:25,210 --> 00:23:26,650
(Bomyeong Clinic)

225
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:29,280
Honey. Honey. Honey, wait.

226
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:31,250
Honey.

227
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:35,680
I can't go back to the way I was.

228
00:24:36,450 --> 00:24:38,180
You still don't really know me.

229
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:39,790
Manager Yu...

230
00:24:40,550 --> 00:24:42,020
has submitted her resignation.

231
00:24:42,460 --> 00:24:44,560
I suggested she take sick leave
or a leave of absence, but...

232
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,360
it seems she's already made up her mind.

233
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:09,980
Kwon Tae Sung.

234
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:17,560
I stopped by on my way to the airport.

235
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:19,730
I'm sorry.

236
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,730
I should have acted sooner.

237
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:25,300
That gunshot before...

238
00:25:27,370 --> 00:25:28,940
I was sent to protect her.

239
00:25:30,140 --> 00:25:32,140
I'm going to be in so much trouble
with Mama when I get back, right?

240
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,110
Is Bo Na going with you?

241
00:25:42,250 --> 00:25:43,780
I know from experience.

242
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:47,590
Just the mention of hurting
her husband or child,

243
00:25:47,990 --> 00:25:50,020
and Yu Bo Na gets that look in her eye.

244
00:25:50,860 --> 00:25:51,990
A person like that...

245
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:54,530
I did try asking her a few times,

246
00:25:55,760 --> 00:25:57,260
but she flat-out refused.

247
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:59,330
It's a shame for the person who's waiting.

248
00:26:05,500 --> 00:26:07,970
When I said I thought
Bo Na had met someone good...

249
00:26:08,980 --> 00:26:10,040
I really meant it.

250
00:26:11,110 --> 00:26:12,880
I told Bo Na the same thing.

251
00:26:13,610 --> 00:26:17,150
She would know that better than anyone.

252
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,150
So...

253
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:27,860
Thank you.

254
00:26:43,140 --> 00:26:44,280
Please handle this with care.

255
00:27:05,260 --> 00:27:09,700
I sent these flowers to Cheol today.
They're called marguerites,

256
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:12,140
but they look a lot like cosmos flowers.

257
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:14,970
That's why our customers
often get them confused.

258
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:17,710
What's the meaning of that flower?

259
00:27:19,910 --> 00:27:21,180
To reveal a secret.

260
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:23,180
True love.

261
00:27:24,050 --> 00:27:26,050
True love has no secrets.

262
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:28,850
Revealing secrets is what makes love true.

263
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:32,260
I used to think that's what it meant,

264
00:27:32,690 --> 00:27:33,760
but someone told me...

265
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:35,530
that the meaning isn't very good.

266
00:27:36,900 --> 00:27:39,530
That sometimes you have secrets
because you love someone too much.

267
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:43,600
He's a person who lives in the light.

268
00:27:44,170 --> 00:27:45,670
We're different people.

269
00:27:47,110 --> 00:27:50,110
If he knew how different we are,
we couldn't be together.

270
00:27:52,610 --> 00:27:53,610
I'm not worried.

271
00:27:54,650 --> 00:27:55,780
Because that won't happen.

272
00:27:57,920 --> 00:28:00,250
The day he sees my other side...

273
00:28:01,850 --> 00:28:03,060
will never come.

274
00:28:04,590 --> 00:28:06,630
At the time, I thought
it was her confidence...

275
00:28:06,690 --> 00:28:08,460
that her secret wouldn't be discovered.

276
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:12,530
But looking back, I think it was anxiety.

277
00:28:15,670 --> 00:28:18,900
Like a promise she made to herself
not to be afraid.

278
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,070
Because she...

279
00:28:21,740 --> 00:28:24,040
knew what would be waiting at the end.

280
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:28,480
I think perhaps from the very beginning,

281
00:28:29,650 --> 00:28:31,050
she had already decided
how she would end things...

282
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:35,150
if a moment like this ever came.

283
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:40,160
That's a thought I had, anyway.

284
00:28:48,670 --> 00:28:51,070
(Comparison of Hair from Sniper Scene
and Deceased's DNA: No Match)

285
00:28:55,470 --> 00:28:56,910
This is Kingfisher Task Force.

286
00:28:59,150 --> 00:29:00,150
Yes, yes.

287
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:03,280
Did we hear back from Interpol?

288
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:05,150
Yes, thank you.

289
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:09,660
Sir, it's the international
cooperation officer.

290
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:12,360
They've found a DNA match
for the body from Russia.

291
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,360
Russia?

292
00:29:14,490 --> 00:29:15,660
(Comparing DNA To Russian Data)

293
00:29:15,730 --> 00:29:16,900
(Identity Confirmed)

294
00:29:17,030 --> 00:29:18,200
Leila Choi.

295
00:29:18,700 --> 00:29:19,930
Thirty-eight years old.

296
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:22,130
Reported missing about 15 years ago.

297
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:24,270
Her whereabouts after that are unknown?

298
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:26,110
Fifteen years...

299
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,170
That overlaps with
when Kingfisher was active, right?

300
00:29:28,840 --> 00:29:30,680
Man, this is undeniable then.

301
00:29:30,840 --> 00:29:32,110
So her name was Leila.

302
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:35,610
Then she must have entered the country
illegally 15 years ago...

303
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:37,220
and has been living
as an undocumented resident.

304
00:29:38,850 --> 00:29:41,190
(Special Investigation Team 1)

305
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:42,720
Isn't that strange?

306
00:29:43,820 --> 00:29:44,820
What is?

307
00:29:45,660 --> 00:29:47,960
The fact that the hair DNA didn't match?

308
00:29:48,760 --> 00:29:52,100
Well, it could have belonged
to an accomplice.

309
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:54,330
That woman, in the middle of the night...

310
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,500
Why did she go to that park alone?

311
00:29:59,570 --> 00:30:00,570
That's a good point.

312
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:02,710
Was she going to meet someone?

313
00:30:03,810 --> 00:30:06,350
But the park was closed then,
so no one else was there.

314
00:30:06,950 --> 00:30:07,950
Exactly.

315
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:11,880
There shouldn't have been anyone there.

316
00:30:16,820 --> 00:30:18,490
Oh, you're home.

317
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:19,860
Yes. Where's Yul?

318
00:30:19,930 --> 00:30:21,660
She's already asleep.
Look what time it is.

319
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:23,230
She'll be sleeping here again tonight.

320
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Mom...

321
00:30:36,780 --> 00:30:38,740
Where did Yul's mother go?

322
00:30:40,910 --> 00:30:43,180
I told you, she went
on a long-term overseas business trip.

323
00:30:43,980 --> 00:30:46,220
- All of a sudden?
- Where overseas?

324
00:30:46,390 --> 00:30:47,390
When is she coming back?

325
00:30:48,290 --> 00:30:50,690
See? Look at his guilty face.

326
00:30:50,860 --> 00:30:51,960
If only he was a better liar.

327
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:54,460
The moment he walked in
with that grim look on his face,

328
00:30:54,530 --> 00:30:56,060
I knew something was up.

329
00:30:56,500 --> 00:30:59,530
Tell me.
What on earth did you do to Bo Na?

330
00:31:00,230 --> 00:31:01,270
- Tell me.
- Tell me.

331
00:31:01,270 --> 00:31:02,300
- Tell me.
- Tell me.

332
00:31:02,300 --> 00:31:04,870
What, did you give her hell
for prioritizing her work over her family?

333
00:31:04,940 --> 00:31:06,910
What century do you think this is?

334
00:31:07,810 --> 00:31:11,280
- He still doesn't get it.
- I'm sure you're the one at fault here.

335
00:31:11,340 --> 00:31:12,410
My point exactly.

336
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,550
When you guys were newlyweds,

337
00:31:14,910 --> 00:31:17,280
I gave her a hard time
because she was clumsy with a knife,

338
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:20,350
and a month later, she came back
with calluses on her hands.

339
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:22,250
Imagine how much she must have
practiced chopping.

340
00:31:22,320 --> 00:31:24,460
I gave her a funny look
when she didn't know who Hyun Bin was,

341
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:25,760
so she went and watched everything
he'd been in.

342
00:31:25,820 --> 00:31:26,960
Then she recited his lines flawlessly.

343
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:29,330
She even asked,
"I'm not weird anymore, am I?"

344
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:31,560
I didn't even ask her to,

345
00:31:31,630 --> 00:31:34,530
but she had her whole department
get every single insurance I sell...

346
00:31:34,530 --> 00:31:36,700
including life, accident, medical,
and long-term care insurance.

347
00:31:37,100 --> 00:31:38,800
I was the top performer that month.

348
00:31:38,870 --> 00:31:40,210
- No way.
- Really?

349
00:31:40,270 --> 00:31:43,410
- Yes.
- That's the kind of person she is.

350
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,880
For someone who tries so hard
at everything...

351
00:31:45,950 --> 00:31:47,750
Imagine how bad things must have been.

352
00:31:48,610 --> 00:31:50,680
She's so devoted to her family.

353
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:52,990
How could she leave Yul behind
and just walk out?

354
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:57,190
My sister-in-law doesn't have any friends.
She'd have nowhere to go.

355
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:00,360
She...

356
00:32:01,030 --> 00:32:03,600
Does she have her own family?
Any blood relatives?

357
00:32:03,730 --> 00:32:06,700
There's no one in this whole world
to take her in.

358
00:32:07,430 --> 00:32:10,870
What in the world did you do
to make her leave home?

359
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:16,280
- Oh no, what should we do?
- Mom.

360
00:32:16,340 --> 00:32:17,440
- Mom, Mom.
- Mom, are you okay?

361
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,780
- Wait.
- Are you okay?

362
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:21,910
- Mom, your blood pressure is rising.
- Mom, calm down.

363
00:32:21,910 --> 00:32:22,920
Mom, your blood pressure can't get high.

364
00:32:22,980 --> 00:32:25,150
Hey, hey, hey. Go get her
blood pressure medicine. Hurry.

365
00:32:25,220 --> 00:32:27,890
- Hurry, hurry. It's over there.
- Mom, are you okay?

366
00:32:27,890 --> 00:32:31,290
When I think about it,
I have so many things to be sorry.

367
00:32:31,290 --> 00:32:32,690
- My wife sure has a lot of supporters.
- Don't be so sad, Mom.

368
00:32:33,230 --> 00:32:35,890
- This is dangerous. So dangerous.
- Let me take a look at it.

369
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:36,960
Why, you...

370
00:32:45,140 --> 00:32:46,510
She doesn't have any family here.

371
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:48,970
{\an8}(8 Years Ago)

372
00:32:49,070 --> 00:32:50,810
She was adopted by a family in Russia
when she was a kid.

373
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:52,780
Then she came back here
once she was an adult.

374
00:33:01,150 --> 00:33:03,490
Be good to her. She's my girlfriend.

375
00:33:03,820 --> 00:33:05,590
Why are you asking me?

376
00:33:06,230 --> 00:33:07,230
It's you who should be good to her.

377
00:33:10,260 --> 00:33:11,730
You said she doesn't have any family.

378
00:33:13,330 --> 00:33:14,400
You better be good to her, man.

379
00:33:25,180 --> 00:33:26,180
I've spotted the suspect.

380
00:33:28,210 --> 00:33:29,280
(Tall, Slender, Short Or Tied Hair,
Red Devils Gear, Big Bag)

381
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:37,690
(Tall, Slender, Short Or Tied Hair,
Red Devils Gear, Big Bag)

382
00:33:40,230 --> 00:33:41,360
(Tall, Slender, Short Or Tied Hair,
Red Devils Gear, Big Bag)

383
00:33:46,370 --> 00:33:47,530
My wife, my child...

384
00:33:48,130 --> 00:33:49,230
The family I love...

385
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:51,900
I have to protect them.

386
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:53,470
You're going to have my back, right?

387
00:33:55,310 --> 00:33:56,380
You said you'd pay me back.

388
00:34:00,780 --> 00:34:05,120
(Municipal Police)

389
00:34:07,990 --> 00:34:09,620
(Not Today)

390
00:34:09,690 --> 00:34:11,690
(Investigative Reporting Team)

391
00:34:14,590 --> 00:34:17,730
Jeez, he must've been really shocked.

392
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:20,900
He's just been totally out of it
since that day.

393
00:34:21,170 --> 00:34:22,170
I know.

394
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:25,300
He just sits there all day
staring at articles about Kingfisher.

395
00:34:26,710 --> 00:34:28,510
Do you think he's stunned
it turned out to be a woman?

396
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:32,780
Or is he just mad
that he missed out on the scoop?

397
00:34:34,580 --> 00:34:35,580
I mean...

398
00:34:35,950 --> 00:34:38,420
He must be upset.
He spent years digging into this.

399
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:40,820
You know,
reporters get like this sometimes.

400
00:34:41,420 --> 00:34:42,420
Just leave him alone for now.

401
00:34:43,990 --> 00:34:45,520
("Live by the Gun, Die by the Gun:
Kingfisher's Tragic End")

402
00:34:45,590 --> 00:34:47,090
("From Arbiter of Justice to Killer:
The Fall of Kingfisher")

403
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:51,930
("Kingfisher's True Face Was That
of a Vicious Killer")

404
00:34:53,970 --> 00:34:56,200
I opened the door
to bring their food into the room,

405
00:34:56,270 --> 00:34:57,640
and the two of them
were whispering secrets...

406
00:34:57,700 --> 00:34:58,700
before they suddenly stopped.

407
00:34:59,370 --> 00:35:00,610
It made me curious,

408
00:35:00,670 --> 00:35:02,740
so I listened
through the door's crack after I left.

409
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:05,410
"Let's do it abroad. Let's meet there."

410
00:35:06,710 --> 00:35:07,910
They were saying something
along those lines.

411
00:35:08,810 --> 00:35:11,520
Did you happen to hear
what it was they were planning to do?

412
00:35:13,490 --> 00:35:15,190
I think they said something
about some girl.

413
00:35:16,790 --> 00:35:18,360
Oh, they said that as long as it is paid,

414
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:19,890
it's all taken care of
with no strings attached.

415
00:35:32,810 --> 00:35:33,840
(Old Marketplace)

416
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:37,110
Oh.

417
00:35:38,110 --> 00:35:39,110
Mr. Kwon Tae Sung.

418
00:35:40,310 --> 00:35:41,310
It's a pleasure to meet you.

419
00:35:41,780 --> 00:35:42,780
Please, come in.

420
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:50,160
Some time ago,

421
00:35:50,420 --> 00:35:53,090
Manager Yu once said she wanted to quit.

422
00:35:53,830 --> 00:35:55,230
At the time, we all begged her to stay.

423
00:35:55,990 --> 00:35:57,330
We thought that if things went on,
Manager Yu...

424
00:35:58,430 --> 00:36:01,170
might die. Everyone was worried.

425
00:36:01,830 --> 00:36:02,870
Manager Yu only...

426
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:06,100
focused on one thing...

427
00:36:07,910 --> 00:36:08,910
as she forged ahead.

428
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:11,940
She thought if she kept at it,

429
00:36:14,010 --> 00:36:16,110
the world would get a little better,

430
00:36:16,820 --> 00:36:18,750
and it would become safer. But...

431
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,420
Does the world really get better
that easily?

432
00:36:24,020 --> 00:36:25,160
That's what...

433
00:36:26,090 --> 00:36:29,700
made Manager Yu the most tired and weary.

434
00:36:34,970 --> 00:36:36,900
Oh, one moment. Wait.

435
00:36:37,670 --> 00:36:39,640
Thinking that we had to save a life,

436
00:36:41,370 --> 00:36:43,140
we sent her on a long vacation.

437
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:45,110
We decided that when she returned,

438
00:36:46,650 --> 00:36:49,620
if she still felt the same way,
we wouldn't try to stop her.

439
00:36:51,050 --> 00:36:52,420
But after 3 or 4 months,

440
00:36:53,390 --> 00:36:54,490
she came back...

441
00:36:55,250 --> 00:36:56,890
and asked me to tear up
her resignation letter.

442
00:37:08,700 --> 00:37:10,100
Even now, I think Manager Yu...

443
00:37:10,700 --> 00:37:12,640
needs that kind of time.

444
00:37:14,110 --> 00:37:15,110
So...

445
00:37:15,470 --> 00:37:18,610
Just think of it as sending her
on a long trip.

446
00:37:20,050 --> 00:37:21,180
If you do,

447
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:24,450
just like you two first met
when she was desperate,

448
00:37:25,820 --> 00:37:27,590
an even greater, desperate opportunity...

449
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:31,520
will come along.

450
00:37:41,130 --> 00:37:42,270
(Detective Lee Dong Jin)

451
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,410
What's up this late at night?

452
00:37:51,940 --> 00:37:53,910
Oh, nothing. I was just thinking of you.

453
00:37:55,210 --> 00:37:56,210
What are you up to?

454
00:37:57,220 --> 00:37:59,890
My wife and Yul said
they wanted ice cream,

455
00:38:00,290 --> 00:38:01,920
so I ran to the convenience store
and am heading home now.

456
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:04,290
Ice cream? In the middle of the night?

457
00:38:05,890 --> 00:38:06,890
That's what they wanted.

458
00:38:10,060 --> 00:38:11,930
Evening practice will be tough for a while
since you're taking care of Yul.

459
00:38:12,730 --> 00:38:13,970
All right, keep in touch.

460
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,440
What about Yul?

461
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:21,010
Se Ah's sister-in-law went away,
so Yul is staying at her place for now.

462
00:38:21,640 --> 00:38:23,210
Bo Na did? Where'd she go?

463
00:38:24,310 --> 00:38:26,580
Her brother said
she's on a long business trip abroad,

464
00:38:27,050 --> 00:38:28,050
but she didn't think so.

465
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:30,350
She is wondering if something happened
between them.

466
00:38:30,920 --> 00:38:32,220
I guess things at home
aren't great these days.

467
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:35,750
Hello.

468
00:38:38,720 --> 00:38:39,730
He calls and then says nothing.

469
00:38:40,390 --> 00:38:42,830
Hello. Lee Dong Jin.

470
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:43,960
Hey.

471
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:47,330
I'm going to ask you
just one very important question,

472
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:48,400
so answer carefully.

473
00:38:51,640 --> 00:38:52,700
What is it now?

474
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:55,570
Who do you like more? Me or your wife?

475
00:38:56,310 --> 00:38:57,510
Are you crazy? Have you been drinking?

476
00:38:58,040 --> 00:38:59,040
I'm being serious right now.

477
00:38:59,310 --> 00:39:00,980
My Bo Na, of course.

478
00:39:01,850 --> 00:39:04,580
I can live happily ever after without you.

479
00:39:04,580 --> 00:39:07,020
But I can't live a single day
without my Bo Na.

480
00:39:07,750 --> 00:39:09,190
Are you serious?

481
00:39:10,260 --> 00:39:11,420
You won't regret that, will you?

482
00:39:11,990 --> 00:39:14,990
Yes. Ask me 100 times.
My answer won't change.

483
00:39:18,130 --> 00:39:20,330
The best thing I've ever done was...

484
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,730
meeting Bo Na,
marrying her, and our family...

485
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:25,370
I mean, building a home together.

486
00:39:33,380 --> 00:39:34,910
I'm hanging up, you psycho.

487
00:40:13,590 --> 00:40:16,350
(Mommy, I Miss You. I Love You A Lot.)

488
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:21,690
(Mommy, I Miss You. I Love You A Lot.)

489
00:40:26,670 --> 00:40:28,070
Which one was your favorite?

490
00:40:28,670 --> 00:40:30,270
All of them.

491
00:40:31,070 --> 00:40:32,470
{\an8}I loved them all. Everything.

492
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,340
{\an8}- It's so nice.
- I think this spot is pretty.

493
00:40:35,410 --> 00:40:36,410
{\an8}- Here?
- Would you like to take a photo here?

494
00:40:37,910 --> 00:40:39,610
Okay, one, two.

495
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:44,780
Stand over there.

496
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:46,320
Me?

497
00:40:46,420 --> 00:40:48,820
Princess Yu Bo Na.

498
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:50,690
Mind your manners.

499
00:40:51,060 --> 00:40:53,390
- It's dangerous, right?
- Okay, strike a pose.

500
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:56,030
One, two, three.

501
00:40:57,730 --> 00:41:01,230
Taking a picture here.
Was today's mission a success?

502
00:41:01,330 --> 00:41:03,700
- Mission accomplished.
- Yes, looks great.

503
00:41:04,740 --> 00:41:08,510
- What should we do next?
- Next?

504
00:41:09,370 --> 00:41:13,950
Make and eat jjajang ramyeon
at home on Sunday.

505
00:41:14,410 --> 00:41:16,350
You know that? On Sunday,
I'm the chef of jjajang ramyeon.

506
00:41:17,380 --> 00:41:18,480
The chef of jjajang ramyeon.

507
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:19,680
All right. What else?

508
00:41:20,050 --> 00:41:23,090
- Get strawberry shakes for dessert.
- Okay.

509
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:26,120
- Watch a late-night movie. Horror movie?
- I'd love to.

510
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,760
- You can handle it, right?
- No.

511
00:41:28,690 --> 00:41:32,130
After that, we'll go for a picnic
at the Han River and eat chicken.

512
00:41:32,260 --> 00:41:34,930
We have so much to do.
We'd better be quick about it.

513
00:41:35,170 --> 00:41:36,570
Is there anything you want to do,
Tae Sung?

514
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:37,640
I want to get married.

515
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:43,280
Well, getting married is still a little...

516
00:41:50,220 --> 00:41:54,990
But when people do this,
they usually prepare something.

517
00:41:56,520 --> 00:41:57,660
This is a proposal, right?

518
00:41:58,620 --> 00:42:01,230
When I see this on TV,
they always give something.

519
00:42:01,230 --> 00:42:05,160
Oh, a ring. The ring. I am sorry.
I mean, this is not a formal proposal.

520
00:42:05,260 --> 00:42:09,400
It was just something
I have been holding back for a long time,

521
00:42:10,170 --> 00:42:11,270
and it just slipped out
without me knowing.

522
00:42:11,340 --> 00:42:13,000
I am going to prepare a formal proposal...

523
00:42:13,570 --> 00:42:16,880
I was planning to give you the ring then.
I'm preparing for all those things.

524
00:42:17,180 --> 00:42:18,180
I see.

525
00:42:22,410 --> 00:42:25,280
But when...

526
00:42:26,490 --> 00:42:27,890
When are you going to do it?

527
00:42:30,490 --> 00:42:32,360
Let me know in advance when you decide.

528
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:36,600
That way, I can also think about
what my answer is going to be.

529
00:42:38,300 --> 00:42:39,930
So let me know the date.

530
00:42:46,670 --> 00:42:48,440
Tae Sung, hurry up.

531
00:42:55,010 --> 00:42:57,450
There are still so many things
I want to do with you.

532
00:42:58,350 --> 00:43:01,750
- Really?
- Things we haven't done yet. Like...

533
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:04,390
Better things, more special things,
things like that.

534
00:43:04,820 --> 00:43:07,830
From now on, let's do them all
1 by 1, together.

535
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:11,630
Okay, together.

536
00:43:51,040 --> 00:43:53,570
(Digging News)

537
00:43:55,540 --> 00:43:56,540
(Investigative Reporting Team)

538
00:43:56,840 --> 00:43:59,410
Sir. Your hunch was right.

539
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:04,450
The two Kingfisher victims
were in Cambodia last summer.

540
00:44:04,450 --> 00:44:05,520
And their time in Cambodia overlaps.

541
00:44:05,920 --> 00:44:06,990
And this.

542
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:09,690
During that time in Cambodia,

543
00:44:09,750 --> 00:44:11,690
a mother and daughter
who sold food on the street...

544
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:13,390
were murdered in another incident.

545
00:44:14,330 --> 00:44:15,830
They were found dead...

546
00:44:17,560 --> 00:44:18,760
and the culprit has not been found.

547
00:44:19,130 --> 00:44:21,730
Please prepare a travel request
for 4 days and 3 nights in Cambodia.

548
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:23,030
Yes, sir.

549
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:26,940
(Detective Lee Dong Jin)

550
00:44:30,610 --> 00:44:31,680
Detective Lee Dong Jin,

551
00:44:32,780 --> 00:44:34,350
let's wrap this case up.

552
00:44:35,250 --> 00:44:36,410
Together.

553
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:49,330
Kwon Se Ah, you still got the moves.

554
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:51,960
Well, my moves to become police officer
are about to come back too.

555
00:44:52,230 --> 00:44:54,400
Jeez, you really underestimate the police.

556
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:56,530
Of course I do.
I know a cop who got thrown...

557
00:44:56,530 --> 00:44:59,440
by a small girl
and whined for her to keep it a secret.

558
00:45:00,010 --> 00:45:01,410
You are still talking about that?

559
00:45:04,980 --> 00:45:06,040
Hey, that was a cheap shot.

560
00:45:06,340 --> 00:45:07,780
That is why you should focus.

561
00:45:15,590 --> 00:45:18,660
- That was close. Focus.
- Hey, I told you not to go easy on me.

562
00:45:19,090 --> 00:45:20,390
Are you doing judo with your mouth?

563
00:45:27,970 --> 00:45:29,030
(Beom Sung Hoon)

564
00:45:35,010 --> 00:45:36,270
(Kwon Se Ah)

565
00:45:48,090 --> 00:45:50,490
Man, I almost died doing judo.

566
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:54,930
Hey, I told you not to do that.

567
00:45:54,930 --> 00:45:56,730
What do you think you are doing
in a sacred dojo?

568
00:45:56,930 --> 00:46:00,300
Hey, what did I do?
You are the one wrestling in a dojo.

569
00:46:00,300 --> 00:46:01,570
You went easy on me, didn't you?

570
00:46:06,500 --> 00:46:09,740
(Kwon Se Ah, Beom Sung Hoon)

571
00:46:16,650 --> 00:46:17,950
Is your tournament preparation going well?

572
00:46:18,550 --> 00:46:21,350
Well, it has been so long
since I quit training,

573
00:46:21,650 --> 00:46:23,420
so I am just getting
the feel for it again.

574
00:46:25,020 --> 00:46:27,060
I thought you could win
even if you competed today.

575
00:46:28,560 --> 00:46:29,660
I saw you with my own eyes.

576
00:46:30,060 --> 00:46:34,130
Well, that was more of a real fight.

577
00:46:34,670 --> 00:46:36,300
A real match is different.

578
00:46:39,470 --> 00:46:41,410
I said I wanted to know
what kind of person you are.

579
00:46:52,120 --> 00:46:53,280
From what I see, you are...

580
00:46:54,320 --> 00:46:56,450
bright, honest, and brave.

581
00:46:57,390 --> 00:46:58,490
And you are upright and proper.

582
00:46:59,860 --> 00:47:02,790
Well, I think you are mostly right.

583
00:47:03,630 --> 00:47:07,330
I think you probably have a rough idea
of who I am too.

584
00:47:08,070 --> 00:47:09,070
So...

585
00:47:10,570 --> 00:47:12,940
I think you're probably thinking
the same thing as me.

586
00:47:14,440 --> 00:47:17,380
The same? What thought?

587
00:47:19,610 --> 00:47:23,010
That we can't have a future together.

588
00:47:24,220 --> 00:47:25,220
That kind of thinking.

589
00:47:28,590 --> 00:47:30,050
I really enjoyed getting
to know you, Se Ah.

590
00:47:30,760 --> 00:47:34,190
I had a wonderful time with you.

591
00:47:37,760 --> 00:47:40,430
You're going to be a great police officer.

592
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:44,840
I'll always be rooting for you from afar.

593
00:48:00,490 --> 00:48:02,850
I promise I'll become
a great police officer.

594
00:48:03,560 --> 00:48:04,960
Thank you, Assistant Manager Ki.

595
00:48:10,700 --> 00:48:13,430
If I go somewhere else again,
will you follow me then too?

596
00:48:13,870 --> 00:48:14,870
Where are you going?

597
00:48:18,670 --> 00:48:21,240
Where would I go? Everything's right here.

598
00:48:21,870 --> 00:48:24,810
She went alone this time.

599
00:48:31,150 --> 00:48:33,890
Stop moping and get up. Quickly.

600
00:48:40,530 --> 00:48:43,060
From now on, let's eat together
at mealtimes.

601
00:48:43,930 --> 00:48:45,200
You have to eat to live.

602
00:48:45,660 --> 00:48:47,600
- I actually eat something.
- A meal.

603
00:48:47,670 --> 00:48:50,600
A proper, warm meal,
not just some junk food to get by.

604
00:48:52,170 --> 00:48:53,970
I eat proper meals sometimes.

605
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:57,010
After we eat, let's go for a walk
in the park nearby.

606
00:48:57,340 --> 00:48:58,340
What?

607
00:48:58,340 --> 00:49:00,550
Don't just coop yourself up
in that smelly little room.

608
00:49:00,610 --> 00:49:02,780
Get some fresh air once in a while. Okay?

609
00:49:04,620 --> 00:49:05,720
I get fresh air sometimes.

610
00:49:06,120 --> 00:49:08,450
After our walk, we're going
clothes shopping.

611
00:49:11,760 --> 00:49:14,290
You have a good frame, at least.

612
00:49:17,900 --> 00:49:19,960
I'm a pretty sharp dresser.

613
00:49:20,900 --> 00:49:22,530
I'm doing all this for myself.

614
00:49:23,130 --> 00:49:24,340
Now that Manager Yu is gone,

615
00:49:24,470 --> 00:49:26,240
think of how often the two of us
will have to go out together.

616
00:49:26,540 --> 00:49:28,040
We need to stay in good shape.

617
00:49:33,910 --> 00:49:35,650
What are you doing?
Your food's getting cold.

618
00:49:36,350 --> 00:49:37,380
Okay.

619
00:49:48,790 --> 00:49:49,860
Mom.

620
00:49:51,460 --> 00:49:55,500
Mom. Mom.

621
00:49:56,070 --> 00:49:58,270
- Mom, where are you?
- Yul, what's wrong?

622
00:49:58,770 --> 00:50:01,140
When is Mom coming home?

623
00:50:04,240 --> 00:50:05,240
Yul.

624
00:50:05,780 --> 00:50:09,180
Mom has so much work
that she's not finished yet.

625
00:50:09,410 --> 00:50:11,980
But I miss Mom.

626
00:50:12,920 --> 00:50:15,690
I guess Mom doesn't miss me.

627
00:50:16,220 --> 00:50:17,360
That's not true.

628
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:21,590
Mom misses you so much
that she cries every night.

629
00:50:21,660 --> 00:50:23,960
- Really?
- Of course.

630
00:50:25,300 --> 00:50:28,630
Yul, Mom misses you too,

631
00:50:28,730 --> 00:50:31,200
but she's being brave and working hard.

632
00:50:32,070 --> 00:50:33,340
So what should you do?

633
00:50:35,970 --> 00:50:37,680
You should be brave
and do well too, right?

634
00:50:38,610 --> 00:50:40,280
That way, when Mom comes home...

635
00:50:42,350 --> 00:50:46,020
When Mom comes home,
she'll see that you bravely...

636
00:50:46,580 --> 00:50:48,890
waited for her,
and she'll be happy, right?

637
00:50:50,890 --> 00:50:54,690
Until then, you have to play well,
eat well, and sleep well.

638
00:50:55,430 --> 00:50:56,790
And I'll work hard at my job.

639
00:50:57,530 --> 00:51:01,130
That way, you and I can be brave together
while we wait for Mom.

640
00:51:02,130 --> 00:51:03,200
How does that sound?

641
00:51:08,870 --> 00:51:10,210
You're such a good girl.

642
00:51:17,880 --> 00:51:19,550
(Siem Reap Murder, Relationship Diagram)

643
00:51:19,550 --> 00:51:20,790
(Oh Seong Nam and Han Deok Man's visit
to Siem Reap)

644
00:51:20,790 --> 00:51:21,950
(Oh Seong Nam And Han Deok Man stayed
in Siem Reap during the same period.)

645
00:51:22,050 --> 00:51:23,150
(Guide's address and link between Oh Seong
Nam and Han Deok Man to be checked)

646
00:51:26,160 --> 00:51:27,930
(Need To Confirm Their Connection)

647
00:51:28,130 --> 00:51:29,930
(Cambodia Reroute, Deep Web Reroute)

648
00:51:34,830 --> 00:51:36,500
(Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic)

649
00:51:36,500 --> 00:51:38,740
Sir, you need to see this.

650
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:42,010
You see "Dr. Oh" and "ChildLover," right?

651
00:51:42,570 --> 00:51:44,280
It's an illegal website. Here and here.

652
00:51:45,210 --> 00:51:46,510
This is evidence related to the case.

653
00:51:46,580 --> 00:51:49,810
It's a document that was faxed over
from the police in Cambodia.

654
00:51:50,180 --> 00:51:51,550
Please take a look.

655
00:51:52,750 --> 00:51:54,050
Dinner's here.

656
00:51:54,720 --> 00:51:56,120
Wow, it looks delicious.

657
00:52:02,260 --> 00:52:04,300
My mom likes chicken porridge too.

658
00:52:04,700 --> 00:52:06,500
Right? Your mom loves chicken porridge.

659
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:08,630
- Yes.
- Am I a good cook?

660
00:52:08,630 --> 00:52:11,300
- Yes, you are.
- Thank you.

661
00:52:18,380 --> 00:52:19,980
Dad, I finished tidying up.

662
00:52:20,310 --> 00:52:21,550
You did all this yourself, Yul?

663
00:52:21,950 --> 00:52:22,950
Good job.

664
00:52:36,460 --> 00:52:38,060
("Kingfisher's Last Two Victims
Were Not Innocent Civilians")

665
00:52:38,130 --> 00:52:41,700
Kingfisher's last two victims
were not innocent civilians.

666
00:52:43,570 --> 00:52:46,570
The shocking truth has been revealed
about the two men...

667
00:52:46,640 --> 00:52:49,340
known as Kingfisher's final victims.

668
00:52:49,740 --> 00:52:52,610
It was believed the two men
had no connection to each other.

669
00:52:52,840 --> 00:52:55,910
But it's been confirmed they were
in a Southeast Asian country...

670
00:52:55,980 --> 00:52:58,080
and staying together at one point.

671
00:52:58,080 --> 00:53:00,380
After investigating the case with a tip
provided by a domestic news outlet...

672
00:53:00,450 --> 00:53:03,290
and the help of local law enforcement,

673
00:53:03,350 --> 00:53:05,490
we uncovered the process
of their criminal plot...

674
00:53:05,560 --> 00:53:07,530
and their act to murder
a mother and daughter.

675
00:53:07,960 --> 00:53:10,960
According to a joint investigation
by a news outlet and the police,

676
00:53:11,100 --> 00:53:14,330
the two men were traveling
in a Southeast Asian country.

677
00:53:14,430 --> 00:53:15,930
They lured and attempted
to sexually assault...

678
00:53:15,930 --> 00:53:18,840
an eight-year-old girl
selling food on the street.

679
00:53:18,900 --> 00:53:21,070
When they failed
because the girl's mother fought back,

680
00:53:21,140 --> 00:53:23,370
they brutally murdered
the mother and daughter...

681
00:53:23,370 --> 00:53:25,940
and abandoned their bodies.

682
00:53:26,010 --> 00:53:29,550
The two men, a practicing doctor
and a middle school teacher,

683
00:53:29,610 --> 00:53:31,780
were sharing child sexual
exploitation material...

684
00:53:31,850 --> 00:53:34,550
as active members
of an illegal online site.

685
00:53:34,620 --> 00:53:36,890
They met offline to plot their crime,

686
00:53:36,950 --> 00:53:40,890
then pretended they were
traveling abroad separately...

687
00:53:40,960 --> 00:53:43,900
before meeting up at the location
to carry it out.

688
00:53:44,960 --> 00:53:47,500
All right, everyone, let's head out.

689
00:53:47,730 --> 00:53:48,800
Let's go.

690
00:53:49,530 --> 00:53:50,570
Let's go.

691
00:53:50,840 --> 00:53:51,840
Right.

692
00:53:57,580 --> 00:53:58,580
Where's Tae Min?

693
00:54:00,040 --> 00:54:01,180
Be safe.

694
00:54:10,450 --> 00:54:12,560
They were long thought
to be innocent civilians...

695
00:54:12,560 --> 00:54:14,260
victimized by Kingfisher.

696
00:54:14,330 --> 00:54:17,260
But as the shocking truth of their crimes
has been revealed,

697
00:54:17,330 --> 00:54:20,400
public opinion on Kingfisher
is shifting once again.

698
00:54:20,600 --> 00:54:22,670
Support is growing for the idea that...

699
00:54:22,730 --> 00:54:25,170
Kingfisher didn't harm
innocent civilians...

700
00:54:28,970 --> 00:54:29,970
That guy.

701
00:54:31,880 --> 00:54:34,380
He really went and
cleared Kingfisher's name.

702
00:54:43,550 --> 00:54:48,530
(Special Investigation Team 1)

703
00:55:05,140 --> 00:55:07,810
I guess I should tidy that up now too.

704
00:55:12,680 --> 00:55:16,120
(Ok's Flower Shop)

705
00:55:17,420 --> 00:55:18,860
As for Yu Bo Na's ending...

706
00:55:20,690 --> 00:55:21,930
I wonder how that will turn out.

707
00:55:30,530 --> 00:55:33,100
{\an8}Yul, I'm working late today,

708
00:55:33,170 --> 00:55:35,770
{\an8}so Aunt Se Ah is going
to pick you up. Okay?

709
00:55:36,510 --> 00:55:39,080
Wash your hands as soon as you get home,

710
00:55:39,140 --> 00:55:43,380
and I've already made the curry you like,
so enjoy it with your aunt.

711
00:55:43,850 --> 00:55:45,880
You can do that, right, sweetheart?

712
00:55:46,120 --> 00:55:47,450
Yes, I can.

713
00:55:48,420 --> 00:55:50,960
- That's my girl.
- The best, the best.

714
00:55:51,390 --> 00:55:54,990
This is how Mom used to do it.
The best, the best.

715
00:55:55,590 --> 00:55:56,690
Your mom did that?

716
00:55:59,100 --> 00:56:01,730
Oh? It's snowing. Dad, look, it's snowing.

717
00:56:02,570 --> 00:56:03,770
Wow, snow.

718
00:56:12,940 --> 00:56:14,250
Want to go outside and see?

719
00:56:18,650 --> 00:56:21,920
Wow, it's snowing so much.

720
00:56:22,390 --> 00:56:25,560
You're right. The first snow
is early this year, isn't it?

721
00:56:25,920 --> 00:56:27,320
Wow, it's so pretty.

722
00:56:34,270 --> 00:56:36,500
My name is Yu Bo Na. That's my real name.

723
00:56:37,030 --> 00:56:38,400
It's a pleasure to meet you.

724
00:56:38,640 --> 00:56:39,970
This is my first time being in love.

725
00:56:46,510 --> 00:56:47,650
It's beautiful.

726
00:57:37,900 --> 00:57:39,830
Do you have any idea
where she could have gone?

727
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:41,570
I'm not sure.

728
00:57:42,700 --> 00:57:44,240
She's always been good at hiding.

729
00:57:45,970 --> 00:57:47,270
She's probably somewhere...

730
00:57:48,710 --> 00:57:50,710
looking for a view of her own.

731
00:57:51,140 --> 00:57:52,810
But she came back 3 or 4 months later...

732
00:57:53,240 --> 00:57:54,850
and asked me to tear up
her resignation letter.

733
00:57:54,910 --> 00:57:56,380
So I asked her why.

734
00:57:57,280 --> 00:57:58,780
And she said just one thing.

735
00:57:59,750 --> 00:58:01,720
That she'd seen a beautiful sight.

736
00:58:02,850 --> 00:58:06,690
I wondered what beautiful sight
she could have seen...

737
00:58:07,190 --> 00:58:10,690
to bring her who was wasting away
back to life like that.

738
00:58:13,800 --> 00:58:15,270
But seeing you, Kwon Tae Sung, I realized.

739
00:58:16,330 --> 00:58:17,540
So you're the one.

740
00:58:18,170 --> 00:58:20,240
The one who saved Manager Yu.

741
00:59:11,060 --> 00:59:15,160
She never used to go outside.
I wonder why she's suddenly going hiking.

742
00:59:15,830 --> 00:59:19,260
Especially on a day like this.
The path must be rough.

743
00:59:42,520 --> 00:59:43,520
Merry Christmas.

744
00:59:44,790 --> 00:59:48,290
This is a Christmas gift for you, Bo Na.

745
00:59:50,260 --> 00:59:51,930
Isn't it so brilliant and beautiful?

746
00:59:53,860 --> 00:59:56,000
I used to suck on these when I was a kid.

747
00:59:56,570 --> 00:59:58,370
We could even make shaved ice
with this, right?

748
01:00:04,910 --> 01:00:06,180
I was so scared...

749
01:00:07,210 --> 01:00:08,580
that you would disappear, Bo Na.

750
01:00:09,980 --> 01:00:11,380
Maybe love...

751
01:00:12,450 --> 01:00:16,220
begins when you fall for just one
of the many sides of a person.

752
01:00:16,220 --> 01:00:17,250
Don't you think so?

753
01:00:17,520 --> 01:00:18,720
For me, it has already begun.

754
01:00:48,920 --> 01:00:49,920
It's beautiful.

755
01:00:52,960 --> 01:00:55,230
This place is definitely more charming
in the winter.

756
01:00:56,030 --> 01:00:57,030
Don't you think?

757
01:01:02,200 --> 01:01:04,500
This field of wildflowers used to be
my favorite view in the world.

758
01:01:04,700 --> 01:01:07,200
But ever since that day,
it changed to this snow-covered field.

759
01:01:07,770 --> 01:01:11,380
I guess your taste in scenery changes
depending on who you're with.

760
01:01:12,480 --> 01:01:14,080
I wonder if the flowers would be sad
to hear that.

761
01:01:20,820 --> 01:01:23,290
The path up was so rough
that it took me a while to get here.

762
01:01:24,120 --> 01:01:26,120
And because of the snow,

763
01:01:26,420 --> 01:01:28,790
I was worried the trail would be closed,

764
01:01:29,560 --> 01:01:31,100
but luckily, the mountain let me pass.

765
01:01:32,660 --> 01:01:35,930
But I still slipped two times
because I was in such a hurry.

766
01:01:35,930 --> 01:01:37,700
I didn't have a chance
to get the proper shoes.

767
01:01:43,610 --> 01:01:44,610
I...

768
01:01:48,380 --> 01:01:49,880
I thought I didn't need to know.

769
01:01:51,120 --> 01:01:52,850
Where you were born or how you grew up.

770
01:01:53,650 --> 01:01:55,920
What you did for work
or how you've lived your life.

771
01:01:55,990 --> 01:01:58,160
All of that... I thought I was fine
not knowing any of it.

772
01:01:58,790 --> 01:02:00,560
Because the Yu Bo Na I know
was enough for me.

773
01:02:02,290 --> 01:02:04,190
The one who now eats chicken
and chicken porridge,

774
01:02:05,730 --> 01:02:09,070
who tells Yul to get along
with her friends every day,

775
01:02:09,900 --> 01:02:10,900
who has a mother,

776
01:02:12,470 --> 01:02:14,570
and even has three aunts.

777
01:02:16,110 --> 01:02:17,310
You're not alone anymore.

778
01:02:19,910 --> 01:02:20,980
I know you so well.

779
01:02:23,310 --> 01:02:26,280
I love you more than anyone else
in the world.

780
01:02:30,550 --> 01:02:31,720
But now I want to know.

781
01:02:35,390 --> 01:02:38,330
What you were feeling
on that long journey here.

782
01:02:39,030 --> 01:02:40,330
How hard it was.

783
01:02:41,670 --> 01:02:43,030
If you were lonely and scared.

784
01:02:43,670 --> 01:02:46,640
I want to know all the sides of you
that I don't know.

785
01:02:55,410 --> 01:02:57,110
I know we can't go back
to how things were.

786
01:02:59,220 --> 01:03:00,350
But let's do this instead.

787
01:03:00,880 --> 01:03:01,990
Let's slowly get to know each other.

788
01:03:03,550 --> 01:03:04,560
Okay?

789
01:03:11,060 --> 01:03:13,030
So I can love every part of who you are,
Yu Bo Na.

790
01:03:33,820 --> 01:03:35,090
Honey, let's go home.

791
01:03:36,490 --> 01:03:37,690
It's too cold out here.

792
01:03:43,260 --> 01:03:44,430
Yul is waiting.

793
01:03:50,900 --> 01:03:53,600
I told her that a wish made
on the first snow comes true,

794
01:03:55,970 --> 01:03:57,980
so she wished to see her mom.

795
01:03:59,710 --> 01:04:00,780
The same as me.

796
01:04:46,020 --> 01:04:47,360
I have a question.

797
01:04:49,660 --> 01:04:50,660
Okay.

798
01:04:56,270 --> 01:04:58,800
- Back during the World Cup,
- Yes?

799
01:04:58,870 --> 01:05:00,240
why did you report me?

800
01:05:01,100 --> 01:05:02,140
Because you were handsome?

801
01:05:05,880 --> 01:05:07,640
You seemed like a good person.

802
01:05:12,150 --> 01:05:15,390
(Taesung Chicken)

803
01:05:19,120 --> 01:05:21,460
(Taesung Chicken)

804
01:05:39,410 --> 01:05:42,380
Geez, why do you keep cleaning
every chance you get?

805
01:05:42,610 --> 01:05:43,850
Are you still that happy about it?

806
01:05:44,180 --> 01:05:45,280
Of course, I am.

807
01:05:45,880 --> 01:05:47,950
I feel like I have everything
in the world.

808
01:05:48,420 --> 01:05:51,220
But the more I think about it,
that landlord is an amazing person.

809
01:05:51,590 --> 01:05:54,690
I mean, how could they sell this shop
for that price?

810
01:05:55,060 --> 01:05:56,060
I know.

811
01:05:56,490 --> 01:05:59,060
I was already grateful
that they never raised the rent.

812
01:05:59,860 --> 01:06:01,400
They're truly a good person.

813
01:06:02,300 --> 01:06:04,230
I thought I'd finally get to see them
at the contract signing,

814
01:06:04,770 --> 01:06:06,000
but they never showed up.

815
01:06:06,470 --> 01:06:07,470
I know.

816
01:06:11,280 --> 01:06:13,140
You always said
your life was in this place,

817
01:06:13,980 --> 01:06:16,310
and now, late in life,
your life is truly blossoming.

818
01:06:16,610 --> 01:06:19,380
You bet. This is really my shop now.

819
01:06:20,450 --> 01:06:22,220
I will...

820
01:06:23,050 --> 01:06:24,250
bet my entire life on this.

821
01:06:24,320 --> 01:06:25,790
Oh, I'm sure you are.

822
01:06:28,760 --> 01:06:31,030
Mom, we're going to be late.

823
01:06:31,090 --> 01:06:33,830
Oh, my. I'm not thinking straight.

824
01:06:34,970 --> 01:06:37,830
Did you pack plenty of snacks and drinks?

825
01:06:37,900 --> 01:06:39,470
- I packed a ton.
- Okay.

826
01:06:39,470 --> 01:06:40,570
Let's hurry up and go.

827
01:06:43,010 --> 01:06:44,980
Let's go.

828
01:06:45,440 --> 01:06:49,110
(Closed in the Morning for a Family Event,
Taesung Chicken)

829
01:06:49,210 --> 01:06:50,880
(Exciting Sports Day)

830
01:06:52,950 --> 01:06:55,220
(Young Dreamers' Unity Festival)

831
01:06:55,290 --> 01:06:56,350
(Kwon Yul)

832
01:06:57,550 --> 01:06:58,560
There she is.

833
01:06:58,560 --> 01:07:00,760
Go, Kwon Yul.

834
01:07:02,730 --> 01:07:06,360
- Go, Blue Team. Go, Blue Team.
- Hye Ri.

835
01:07:08,200 --> 01:07:09,200
Go, go.

836
01:07:10,030 --> 01:07:11,030
You got it, you got it.

837
01:07:14,400 --> 01:07:15,610
(Our Family's Little Treasure)

838
01:07:17,470 --> 01:07:18,540
(You Did Well.)

839
01:07:18,540 --> 01:07:20,110
Mom, I got first place.

840
01:07:20,180 --> 01:07:21,280
My daughter's the best.

841
01:07:21,810 --> 01:07:23,180
Daddy's treasure is the best.

842
01:07:23,250 --> 01:07:25,780
See? That national athlete blood
from her aunt runs deep.

843
01:07:26,080 --> 01:07:27,880
What do you mean, your blood?

844
01:07:27,950 --> 01:07:30,190
Oh, she must be happy
her mom and dad are here together.

845
01:07:30,250 --> 01:07:34,830
- Our Yul is just flying around today.
- Kwon Yul is the best.

846
01:07:35,060 --> 01:07:38,100
Okay, next up is the parent relay race.

847
01:07:41,630 --> 01:07:43,670
See the calf muscles on number one
from the other team?

848
01:07:45,400 --> 01:07:48,910
- That mom does PT three times a week.
- Three times.

849
01:07:48,970 --> 01:07:50,170
She has a fast start.

850
01:07:50,670 --> 01:07:53,310
And number two keeps shifting her weight
to her left foot.

851
01:07:53,710 --> 01:07:54,980
That means her knee is bad.

852
01:07:55,280 --> 01:07:56,280
Okay.

853
01:07:57,010 --> 01:07:58,950
She'll slow down on the corners.

854
01:07:59,420 --> 01:08:02,150
Number three, in particular,
is a dangerous one.

855
01:08:02,350 --> 01:08:04,090
- Why? Why?
- Why?

856
01:08:04,960 --> 01:08:06,560
Go, Sol's Mom.

857
01:08:06,960 --> 01:08:08,530
- Mom.
- Looking good.

858
01:08:08,590 --> 01:08:10,760
People like that are
incredibly competitive.

859
01:08:11,130 --> 01:08:12,830
She'll go nuts when she gets the baton.

860
01:08:13,830 --> 01:08:15,830
And the last one over there, number five.

861
01:08:16,500 --> 01:08:19,040
She came in heels
and just changed into sneakers.

862
01:08:19,800 --> 01:08:23,710
- No way, what do we do?
- That means, "You're all dead today."

863
01:08:24,780 --> 01:08:25,780
That's what that means.

864
01:08:27,010 --> 01:08:28,980
Okay, then I'll be the anchor.

865
01:08:29,480 --> 01:08:30,980
Because finishing things off
is my specialty.

866
01:08:31,350 --> 01:08:32,350
Okay.

867
01:08:33,080 --> 01:08:34,990
All right. Ready to do this?

868
01:08:35,250 --> 01:08:37,650
- Go for the kill.
- You got this.

869
01:08:40,090 --> 01:08:42,290
- Go.
- Go, Blue Team.

870
01:08:48,270 --> 01:08:49,970
(Red Team, Blue Team)

871
01:08:53,740 --> 01:08:54,740
Ready.

872
01:09:01,410 --> 01:09:02,410
(Go, Seong Yun, Go.)

873
01:09:03,050 --> 01:09:04,050
(Exciting Sports Day)

874
01:09:05,120 --> 01:09:06,720
Here, take it. Take it. Take it.

875
01:09:11,090 --> 01:09:12,090
Hye Ri's mom.

876
01:09:17,430 --> 01:09:18,430
(Go, Sol's Mom.)

877
01:09:21,200 --> 01:09:23,170
Go, Seo Jun's mom.

878
01:09:25,900 --> 01:09:27,200
Is she really running like that?

879
01:09:27,800 --> 01:09:28,810
What is she doing?

880
01:09:30,440 --> 01:09:33,810
- She's all talk.
- Good, good. You got it.

881
01:09:33,810 --> 01:09:34,850
You got it.

882
01:09:34,850 --> 01:09:38,250
- Come on, let's go.
- Let's go.

883
01:09:45,060 --> 01:09:46,320
(We're Cheering For You)

884
01:09:54,400 --> 01:09:55,400
(Young Dreamers' Unity Festival)

885
01:10:10,150 --> 01:10:11,150
Hurry.

886
01:10:14,350 --> 01:10:15,720
Wow, the anchor is running...

887
01:10:15,790 --> 01:10:17,390
- at an incredible speed.
- What's with that mom?

888
01:10:17,520 --> 01:10:20,490
- She's closing the distance.
- Go, Yu Bo Na.

889
01:10:20,490 --> 01:10:23,690
- The anchor has one more lap.
- Go.

890
01:10:56,290 --> 01:11:00,030
- Did I just see that?
- Yul gets that from his mom.

891
01:11:00,160 --> 01:11:02,170
I wonder what she did back in the day.

892
01:11:03,100 --> 01:11:05,300
That's a total waste of talent.

893
01:11:05,470 --> 01:11:08,740
I'm so proud of my daughter-in-law.

894
01:11:30,590 --> 01:11:31,600
You scared me.

895
01:11:31,760 --> 01:11:36,070
- You're slacking off instead of working?
- Oh, come on.

896
01:11:38,500 --> 01:11:39,840
I'm not slacking off.

897
01:11:41,610 --> 01:11:43,570
I'm just taking a break from the sun.

898
01:11:44,110 --> 01:11:45,340
I felt like I was going
to burn to a crisp.

899
01:11:45,440 --> 01:11:47,640
Why do you make things so hard
for yourself?

900
01:11:47,910 --> 01:11:50,410
You turned down a special promotion
and a reward.

901
01:11:50,710 --> 01:11:53,350
You're probably the first detective
to ever ask for a demotion.

902
01:11:53,780 --> 01:11:54,780
Look who's talking. Jeez.

903
01:11:55,120 --> 01:11:56,550
Hey, is it common
for a reporter to turn down...

904
01:11:56,620 --> 01:11:57,820
the Journalist of the Year award?

905
01:12:04,530 --> 01:12:06,500
The world is still full of bad guys.

906
01:12:06,930 --> 01:12:08,970
That's why we're getting so much crap.

907
01:12:10,070 --> 01:12:11,530
They want Kingfisher back.

908
01:12:12,140 --> 01:12:15,840
People always long for
what's no longer there.

909
01:12:16,470 --> 01:12:19,140
Well, they should look for that
in fantasy novels.

910
01:12:19,580 --> 01:12:22,380
That's why you should go back to your post
and do your job, okay?

911
01:12:22,810 --> 01:12:25,180
Do a good job
so another one isn't born into this world.

912
01:12:26,320 --> 01:12:27,320
I will.

913
01:12:32,460 --> 01:12:34,190
You should worry about doing your own job,
Kwon Tae Sung.

914
01:12:35,330 --> 01:12:36,530
I always do my job.

915
01:12:42,500 --> 01:12:43,500
What is that?

916
01:12:46,100 --> 01:12:47,100
Jeez.

917
01:13:10,230 --> 01:13:11,460
(Three Bears)

918
01:13:40,760 --> 01:13:43,390
This morning, a woman in her 30s
was found dead...

919
01:13:43,460 --> 01:13:46,000
from stab wounds
in a residential area of Seoul.

920
01:13:46,160 --> 01:13:50,470
Police believe a man in his 40s
who served time for stalking the woman...

921
01:13:50,470 --> 01:13:52,170
was released
from prison and held a grudge...

922
01:13:52,240 --> 01:13:55,270
against her for reporting him,
and murdered her in an act of revenge.

923
01:13:55,410 --> 01:13:58,010
They announced they are currently
tracking the fugitive.

924
01:13:58,580 --> 01:14:00,440
The victim had told friends and family...

925
01:14:00,580 --> 01:14:03,010
{\an8}that she believed he would come for her
after his release,

926
01:14:03,080 --> 01:14:06,150
{\an8}and reportedly suffered
from extreme anxiety.

927
01:14:06,750 --> 01:14:09,690
Amidst growing public anxiety
over repeated crimes related to revenge,

928
01:14:09,790 --> 01:14:13,090
the police are focusing their efforts
on apprehending the suspect.

929
01:14:14,720 --> 01:14:15,730
Yes.

930
01:14:19,160 --> 01:14:21,160
Okay, shall we?

931
01:15:24,030 --> 01:15:28,130
(A Bona fide Killer)

932
01:15:28,970 --> 01:15:30,530
{\an8}(Thanks to Lee Elijah, Choi Duk Moon,
Kim Hye Sun, And Jang Eun Sil...)

933
01:15:30,530 --> 01:15:32,440
{\an8}(For Cameo Performance)

934
01:16:18,680 --> 01:16:20,080
{\an8}(Thank You To Our Viewers.)

935
01:16:20,150 --> 01:16:22,020
{\an8}(We Hope You Find
Your Own Beautiful Scenery.)
